    "created_at": "2025-12-10T22:00:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-10T22:15:11Z",
    "body": "I also noticed in my case that Starship's special fonts don't work when starting the Raspberry Pi CUI (tty), \nand I was researching this. As mentioned here, I came up with a method to try not to start it when it's a tty using a bash if statement, or to start it with a different profile.\nHowever, in my case, I used kmscon, which is a tty replacement (unicode compatible), and set the font, and it was successful in displaying the font, although it was a little off.\n_Refer to the archlinux wiki and add the results found with ```fc-list -v | grep Nerd``` to 99-kmscon.conf_\n Rather than fixing the display issue on starship's tty, this is replacing the tty with something else :)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
