    "created_at": "2026-03-04T14:53:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-04T14:58:53Z",
    "body": "Hello, I'm also encountering the same issue with home-manager https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/issues/8841.\n\nHome-manager uses nix to template the shell initialization script, so it's not possible to use the default way provided by upstream to configure starship integration without working around it (writing the integration script oneself and guard it behind an if).\n \nWould love to see starship deactivate some features when used in tty. Maybe it can be turned off completely, or some features like true color and nerd fonts glyphes can be disabled?\n\nThank you for your time :)",
